  "output_text": "**Introduction/Context**  \nThe study investigates the functional role of circRMST in neuroendocrine prostate cancer (NEPC) using SHP77 cells. circRMST knockdown via shRNAs targeting the backspliced junction led to impaired cell growth, cell-cycle arrest, and reduced tumor growth in vivo. RNA-seq identified differentially expressed genes (DEGs) following knockdown. Dataset references: Teng et al., 2025 (Cancer Cell).  \n\n**Keywords**  \ncircRMST, neuroendocrine prostate cancer (NEPC), SHP77 cells, RNA-seq, differentially expressed genes (DEGs), GSEA, pathway enrichment, cell-cycle arrest, tumor growth inhibition.  \n\n**Candidate Genes**  \nASCL1, GRP, CD24, DHRS2, FN1, TRPM8, SOX11, ID2, PTBP3, EIF3I.  \n\n**Pathway Enrichments**  \nGSEA results were not provided in the uploaded datasets. The analysis focused on DEG lists but lacked pathway-level enrichment data (e.g., KEGG, GO). Without GSEA outputs, pathway-level conclusions cannot be drawn.  \n\n**Targeted (Keyword-Guided) Subset**  \nNo pathway enrichment data available for filtering.  \n\n**Key Genes/Proteins (Leading Edge)**  \n| Gene    | Direction | Role/Function                          | Pathway(s)                |  \n|---------|-----------|----------------------------------------|---------------------------|  \n| **ASCL1**   | Down      | Neuroendocrine differentiation, transcription factor | Neurogenesis, NEPC progression |  \n| **GRP**     | Down      | Neuroendocrine marker, mitogenic signaling | Gastrin-releasing peptide pathway |  \n| **CD24**    | Down      | Cell adhesion, metastasis              | Cancer progression        |  \n| **DHRS2**   | Down      | Retinol metabolism, tumor suppression  | Retinoic acid signaling   |  \n| **TRPM8**   | Down      | Calcium channel, NEPC progression      | Calcium signaling         |  \n\n**Comparisons**  \nNot applicable due to lack of pathway data.  \n\n**Implications**  \nDownregulation of **ASCL1**, **GRP**, and **TRPM8** aligns with impaired neuroendocrine features and tumor growth, suggesting circRMST regulates NEPC-specific oncogenic programs.  \n\n**Next Steps & Clarification**  \n1. Perform GSEA using the provided DEG lists to identify enriched pathways.  \n2. Validate the role of **ASCL1** and **TRPM8** in NEPC models post-circRMST knockdown.  \n3. Clarify if cell-cycle arrest is directly linked to retinoic acid signaling (DHRS2) or calcium dysregulation (TRPM8).  \n\n**References**  \nNot applicable (no PMIDs validated in current analysis).  \n\n---  \n**Critical Limitation**: The uploaded datasets lack GSEA results, preventing pathway-level interpretation. The nominated target **ASCL1** is prioritized due to its established role in NEPC and concordant downregulation across shRNAs.",
